t commit 5754940 (runs.db)"}, "_lifecycle_floor": "observation"}, {"id": "F-03", "tier": "mechanism", "mechanism_origin": "emergent", "statement": "The fraction-volume trend follows from a shared compensation, not from different responses per patient. Every patient runs Pulse's same baroreflex (F-01), and the absolute loss is much less variable (1094-1755 mL) than the starting volume (2881-7072 mL); because a similar absolute loss is taken from very different reserves, the fraction lost falls as starting volume rises (rho = -0.91). The uniform mechanism, not patient-specific physiology, produces the correlation.", "evidence": {"study_tests": ["tests/test_cohort.py::test_every_patient_bleeds_and_compensates", "tests/test_cohort.py::test_smaller_patients_lose_a_larger_fraction"], "runs": "canonical runs: investigation run of 2026-10-23 at commit 5754940 (runs.db)"}, "_lifecycle_floor": "candidate-explanation"}], "alternative_hypotheses": [{"hypothesis": "The fraction-volume correlation is driven by one or two outlier patients.", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "The correlation is Spearman (rank-based) over all 21 patients, rho = -0.91, which is not set by a single extreme value."}, {"hypothesis": "Larger patients lose a larger fraction, or there is no relationship.", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "The rank correlation is strongly negative (-0.91); smaller patients lose the larger fraction (F-02)."}, {"hypothesis": "Some patients do not compensate (a qualitatively different response).", "status": "excluded", "evidence": "F-01 \u2014 all 21 patients bled, lost volume and raised heart rate, and none reached an irreversible state."}], "discovery_implications": {"resolved": "Across Pulse's 21 shipped patients the bleed-and-compensate response is qualitatively uniform, and the fraction lost falls with starting blood volume.", "remaining": "Whether this holds for a real population rather than Pulse's shipped examples, and whether one severity means the same bleeding rate across body sizes.", "followup_study_proposals": [{"title": "cohort-no-bleed-control", "motivation": "Run the no-bleed arm for all 21 patients so the negative control is cohort-wide rather than borrowed from the StandardMale sibling run."}, {"title": "severity-calibrated-to-flow", "motivation": "Map Pulse severity to a per-patient flow rate so equal severity means equal bleeding rate, isolating body size from bleed rate."}]}, "conclusion": "## Claims\nThe hypothesis holds (23/23 tests passed).\n\n## Limitations\nThe shipped patients are examples, not a population, and the same severity is not the same bleeding rate in every patient.\n", "interface": {"composite": null, "config": {}, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "emitter": null}, "feedback_tracked": {"items": [], "summary": {"open": 0, "addressed": 0, "dismissed": 0, "total": 0}}, "feedback_actions": {"items": [], "summary": {"open": 0, "applied": 0, "dismissed": 0, "total": 0}}, "derived_status": {"simulation_status": {"value": "ran", "source": "21 completed run(s)"}, "evaluation_status": {"value": "evaluated", "source": "completed run + recorded verdicts"}}, "clarity_summary": {"ran": {"status": "ran", "n_runs": 21, "latest": null, "label": "Ran \u00b7 21 runs"}, "tests": {"total": 2, "pass": 0, "fail": 0, "skip": 0, "pending": 2, "label": "Tests: 2\u23f3"}, "verdict": {"value": "passed", "label": "Passed", "glyph": "\u2705", "cls": "v-pass"}, "ambiguities": ["ran, but every test renders 'pending' \u2014 no run outcomes recorded (add runs[].outcomes so the tests show pass/fail)"]}, "computed_gate_verdict": {"result": "blocked", "blocked_by": ["every-patient-compensates", "smaller-patients-lose-larger-fraction"], "evaluated_by": "code", "diverges_from_authored": false, "counts": {"total": 2, "pass": 0, "fail": 0, "skip": 0, "pending": 2}}, "verdict_count_split": {"regression_pins": {"total": 0, "pass": 0, "fail": 0}, "acceptance_criteria": {"total": 0, "pass": 0, "fail": 0}, "expected_fail": {"total": 0, "behaved